# "Target creature gains..." is not limited to your creatures, and the ability belongs to the creature, so its
# controller activates it (and needs it not summoning sick: Bot2's Ornithopter has been there since turn 2).
# Bot1 gives Bot2's Ornithopter the ability on turn 4 and Bot2 uses it to return Bot1's Ornithopter to Bot1's hand;
# Bot1's own Ornithopter has no ability to activate.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Banishing Knack
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Banishing Knack.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Island
Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot1.Graveyard = Banishing Knack
